Always log the formats the video appsink accepts

flutter-pi restricts the appsink's caps to formats EGL can import as
DMA-BUF. When that list is empty the caps are empty, no decoder pad can
link, and playback hangs forever with only a GStreamer "delayed linking
failed" warning - the actual reason is only printed at debug level.

Print the format count and the resulting caps unconditionally, once per
player, so the cause is on the console instead of behind a debug build.

Signed-off-by: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/player.c
+++ b/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/player.c
@@ -928,6 +928,15 @@
         gst_caps_append(caps, gst_caps_new_simple("video/x-raw", "format", G_TYPE_STRING, gst_video_format_to_string(gst_format), NULL));
     }
     gst_app_sink_set_caps(GST_APP_SINK(sink), caps);
+    {
+        // Mira: always say what the sink accepts. When EGL offers no importable
+        // format these caps are empty, no decoder pad can link, and playback
+        // hangs with only a 'delayed linking failed' warning to go on.
+        gchar *caps_str = gst_caps_to_string(caps);
+        fprintf(stderr, "[gstreamer video player] %d importable formats, appsink caps: %s\n",
+                frame_interface_get_n_formats(player->frame_interface), caps_str);
+        g_free(caps_str);
+    }
     gst_caps_unref(caps);

     gst_app_sink_set_callbacks(
